WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.720 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my name is Johanna Stowe and this is my  life in pictures I grew up in Malaysia  in a small town called Tran Ghana which  is located in Southeast Asia  and most well known for its beautiful  beaches and Islands my parents met got  married and they had my brother two  years later they brought me into this  world on the 22nd of September when my  parents had me everyone around them  thought they had given birth to another  baby boy because I had very little hair  up to five years oh I guess that's the  reason for my mom to dress and doll me  up just so I would look like a little  girl my dad owns a small local furniture  shop and my mom was a primary school  teacher my dad is a pet lover and  growing up we had many dogs in our home  there was once where we had up to ten  dogs but of course we had to give them  away I would turn together has always  been with nature we would swim in the  river or Beach go camping together and  basically just to experience the  traditional life of my town growing up  my parents had very little but they have  always worked very hard to give us the  best of what they can my mom would get  us involved with dancing and acting  performances in our local church and she  would save art and send us for piano  lessons it has always been a dream to  play the piano but she just did not have  the privilege to as a child so she  wanted to provide us with as many  different opportunities as possible so  as a team I played the keyboards guitar  and bass in my church I was a write  tomboy then and I still am in a way my  mom has always dreamt of graduating with  a degree but with the lack of funding  she couldn't afford to further her  studies that however never stopped her  with the monthly savings that she made  as a teacher and with my father's  support she pursued law through distant  learning and eventually graduated it was  a challenging path for our  especially being Asian most Asians  mentality is that once you're married as  a woman it is your duty to care for your  family and in a way to leave all your  dreams behind so she didn't receive much  support from her friends and external  family members when she finally  graduated we went to London together for  her graduation and to visit other parts  of Europe that was my family's first  vacation together abroad my parents only  had enough savings to pay for the air  tickets accommodation and food so all  the winter clothings were borrowed from  other family members notice the  oversized jackets my brother and I had  on one thing my mom has taught me is  never be afraid to dream and it's never  too late to pursue your dreams when  opportunities do not come your way make  it own path and create your own  opportunities I am extremely proud of  her  following in my parents footsteps I have  always been adventurous and sick to  learn and experience as much as I can in  life so at the age of 15 I went to Japan  under a student exchange program where I  experienced the Japanese culture for  three weeks with two lovely host  families I went to the school met the  town's mayor wore a kimono and even gave  my first Japanese speech since then I  aim to visit one new country every year  and to keep discovering the beautiful  world around me one of the unforgettable  adventures was my first bungee jump in  New Zealand I chickened out and the  instructor had to push me off the cliff  it was extremely terrifying for me would  I do it again probably in 10 years time  or never in high school I had three best  girlfriends we would pretty much do  everything together I was enrolled in  the science classes because in Malaysia  studying science is deemed to have a  more promising future I was never really  interested in the subjects and so my  only drive to go to school was because  of my involvement in my school drama  team that's the only thing I really look  forward to every day so when I graduated  from high school I knew I wanted to  to performing arts the people around me  hugely discouraged me and consider it to  be a waste of my career because I  graduated with pretty good results you  were taught to study hard to be a doctor  lawyer accountant engineer basically the  typical jobs that most Asians called  secure and highly respected I went  against the norm and enrolled to pursue  theater and film instead I was blessed  to have the full support from both my  parents to pursue what I wanted because  most of my friends had to study what  their parents thought was best for them  and not what they truly wanted so at the  age of 17 I left my town to go to  college in the capital of Malaysia Kuala  Lumpur it's always a dream for someone  who is from a small child to go to a big  city I met a new group of friends  started discovering myself even more and  did many different things I did modeling  film acting theater acting but one thing  that would change my life forever was  when I started going to the gym because  I was called pleasantly plump and  eventually I enrolled to be certified as  a personal trainer whilst still in  college I then started training with  Fitness fest Malaysia and eventually  resigned when I arrived to further my  degree in the UK this was another big  step in my life to leave everyone I knew  behind to go to an unknown place I had  no idea what my future lies for me but I  father need to expand to learn and to  experience more so as I was searching  and praying something inside me tell me  that I should go to the UK to complete  my degree and start there I have always  listened to my gut feelings and have  faith that everything would work out for  the best my parents did not have the  full fund to support my studies to the  UK it was expensive as our Malaysian  currency is very low one pound equals  five ringgit so that's five times at the  amount of everything so we applied for a  local scholarship having faith that I  would be accepted if it's meant for me  to go to the UK which I did yes  and with some money saved up from my  personal training I flew there on  September 2010  in the UK I worked part-time as a  fitness instructor to partially support  myself and eventually graduated after  graduation the dream was to go to London  and get a job in TV production which I  did I applied for a job as a TV producer  and worked in London for nine months but  it wasn't as rewarding because I felt  the need to connect with people which is  why I love fitness training I can't  really remember how I stumble upon the  idea of filming YouTube videos but I  remember telling my mom that I would  like a video camera for my birthday and  that I would start filming my workout  videos and posted them online  my mum had no idea how it would work  neither did I all I knew was that I had  to connect with all of you around the  world and to share my passion for  healthy living I knew how to film and  edit so why not take this risk I thought  to myself what do I have to lose do I  want to stay stuck in a job and  environment I don't enjoy just to  survive or would I take this risk and go  on this adventure and see where it will  lead me so I told my mom to give me one  year to make this work and as always my  parents have been very supportive in my  decisions  I created my job took the courage to  film edited posted and shared my very  first workout video on the 28th of  February I remember being really nervous  and I still AM to see the response that  I'll get obviously no one knew about me  or my videos but I just kept going  having faith that eventually I'll be  able to share my personal fitness and  life journey with all of you I strive to  improve myself learn from the feedback I  received and most importantly to connect  with all of you personally I would spend  hours sometimes even up to eight hours  just sitting in front of my laptop reply  to all your comments as much as I am  sharing my life fitness journey and  knowledge with you I am learning and  discovering even more about myself  through all your comments questions  encouragement and love my life is always  changing and evolving so it  is very important for us to count our  blessings every day one thing I know is  that I love making videos to inspire and  connect with all of you this is just the  beginning of my new chapter and this is  something I'll keep doing I am blessed  with a family that supports my dreams  and decisions even when I do not know  what I'm doing or when others discourage  me my parents have always taught me to  pray trust in your instincts and have  faith that life will guide you to your  purpose and now I have you guys no  matter where you're at in your life  right now  never stop learning discovering and most  importantly to take charge of your  emotions and life you are the creator of  your own destiny  I love you guys  [Music]  you

